WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.520
Siti, a fictional migrant worker, is opening a bank account.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.130
The bank's AI agent wants her records.

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:08.760
How much should it get to see?

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:16.000
Her facts are signed when they happen: on payday, the factory signs her hours, and so does Siti.

00:00:16.350 --> 00:00:20.030
Change one number later, and the signatures no longer match.

00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:24.950
In the demo: one tap, and every card is signed by both.

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:29.870
The agent can only get yes-or-no answers, so Siti allows it.

00:00:30.220 --> 00:00:37.260
Then three gates, in order: who is asking, is the evidence genuine, and may this be asked?

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.993
Same evidence, two agents.

00:00:39.993 --> 00:00:44.860
The bank's gets three yeses and a recommendation for a person to approve.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:50.601
A brand's agent gets one group number: 85 percent across 20 workers.

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:51.790
No one's hours.

00:00:52.790 --> 00:00:55.900
That's exactly what the demo shows, side by side.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.370
When Siti leaves the country, all her cards are revoked at once.

00:01:01.720 --> 00:01:05.130
Gate two now stops the bank's agent before it reads anything.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.900
Refused, with nothing read.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:11.890
Then the team attacks it.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:19.190
A planted note changes no answer: no language model makes the decision, and a summary that contradicts it is dropped.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:24.237
And two queries that single out five workers by subtraction?

00:01:24.237 --> 00:01:25.670
The second is refused.

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:30.860
Evidence at Source: the agents get answers, not data.
